  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, thanks for letting us know. I checked your laptop (BL-LT-0101) and it doesn't look low on space right now. It has about 310 GB free out of 512 GB, which is around 60%, and it isn't showing any storage warnings on our side. That means no cleanup is needed at the moment. To find out what you saw, could you tell us: (1) the exact wording of the message, or send a screenshot, (2) whether it named a drive, like C: or a USB or external drive, and (3) whether it was a Windows notification or a pop-up in your web browser. If it was a browser pop-up asking you to click, call a number, or download a 'cleaner', please don't click it. Close the browser and let us know. If the warning was real and comes back, here's how to free up space: empty the Recycle Bin and your Downloads folder, then go to Settings > System > Storage > Temporary files and remove them. Once we hear back from you, we'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "User is the CEO (VIP), ticket is P3. Checked device BL-LT-0101 per KB-017: online, last check-in 2026-10-09 14:58 UTC, 512 GB total, 310 GB free (60.5%), no warnings. That's well above the 10% threshold, so the report doesn't match the device data. Possible causes: an external or secondary drive, a warning that has already cleared, the wrong device, or a browser scareware pop-up. Asked the user for the exact message or a screenshot, the drive, and where it appeared. No cleanup or escalation needed unless they come back with evidence of a real low-space problem. If it was a scareware pop-up and they clicked anything, treat it as a security issue and escalate.",
